 "equipment_type": "Fluid cooler / cooling tower control panel (1-4 cells)",
 "applies_to": "EVAPCO fluid cooler units controlled by the Sage water and energy conservation control panel, for one to four cells.",
 "summary": "The Sage PLC panel runs EVAPCO fluid cooler cells: pumps, fans on VFDs, make-up water, basin heaters, louver de-icing and lead/lag between cells. It talks BACnet MS/TP on its RS-485 port (or Modbus RTU, chosen at the HMI) and BACnet IP on its Ethernet port. The BMS can enable the system, send a leaving fluid setpoint, acknowledge alarms and must toggle a heartbeat object.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Objects are numbered for cells 1-4; objects for cells that are not installed have no meaning. Cell 1 and cell 2 have more objects than cells 3 and 4.",
  "Temperatures are in 0.1 °F (850 = 85.0 °F) and fan speeds in 0.1 %.",
  "The guide prints BINARY_VALUE 109 twice: bnC4DischargeDamper (cell 4 damper status) and bnBMSHeartbeat. Only the first is listed here; check which one the panel serves before mapping the heartbeat.",
  "The guide warns that non-volatile objects (setpoints, configuration) are rated for about 100,000 writes; do not write them cyclically.",
  "BACnet MS/TP and Modbus RTU share the serial port; only one runs at a time. BACnet IP and BACnet MS/TP are not available at the same time."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "Operations & Maintenance Instructions Addendum - Communications Guide for Sage Water & Energy Conservation Control System",
  "doc_number": null,
  "revision_date": "Revision 1.3",
  "url": "https://www.evapco.com/media/1962586"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Pick BACnet MS/TP or Modbus RTU for the serial port at the HMI (BACnet IP uses the Ethernet port; IP and MS/TP are not available together). Write bnEnableSystem to enable the system and bnBASSP for the leaving fluid setpoint, and keep the BMS heartbeat toggling. Monitor bnSYSEnabled, bnLocalRemoteStatus, the common leaving temperature, cell fan speeds and the alarm flags; bnALM_ACK acknowledges alarms.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BV 35",
    "name": "bnEnableSystem",
    "why": "System enable from the BMS (1 = enabled)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 24",
    "name": "bnBASSP",
    "why": "Leaving fluid setpoint, 0.1 °F (850 = 85.0 °F)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 36",
    "name": "bnALM_ACK",
    "why": "Acknowledge alarms (1 = acknowledge)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 25",
    "name": "bnLocalRemoteStatus",
    "why": "Control mode: 0 local, 1 remote"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 26",
    "name": "bnSYSEnabled",
    "why": "System enabled status"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 52",
    "name": "bnActiveSetpoint",
    "why": "Active fluid setpoint in use, 0.1 °F"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 30",
    "name": "bnCommonLeavingTemp",
    "why": "Average leaving fluid temperature, 0.1 °F"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 28",
    "name": "bnC1VFDSpeed",
    "why": "Cell 1 fan speed, 0.1 %"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 21",
    "name": "bnC1VFDFaultALM",
    "why": "Cell 1 VFD fault alarm"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 103",
    "name": "bnHighCommonTempALM",
    "why": "High common supply water temperature alarm"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "bnEnableSystem (BV 35) enables the system from the BMS; bnLocalRemoteStatus shows whether the panel is in local or remote control.",
  "heartbeat": "The guide lists bnBMSHeartbeat: 0 means waiting for the PLC to set it to 1 (5 s), 1 means waiting for the BMS to write it back to 0 (30 s). The guide does not say what the panel does when the BMS misses it. It is printed with the same instance as another object (BV 109), so confirm the live object before mapping it.",
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "Default communication parameters are printed on the Network Wiring page of the panel wiring schematic.",
   "The serial protocol (BACnet MS/TP or Modbus RTU) is chosen in the HMI Operator Menu.",
   "Modbus TCP stays active on the Ethernet port alongside BACnet IP."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "Do not write setpoints or other non-volatile objects cyclically; the memory is rated for about 100,000 writes.",
   "Runtime reset objects (pump/fan runtime reset) are writable and clear the hour counters.",
   "Temperatures are tenths of a degree F."
  ]
 },
